# howto.domain-discovery

## .what
surface a domain's true objects, operations, and ubiqlang before/while you model them in code
find what exists in the domain and what to call it, so code speaks the domain's own words

## .why
- code that speaks ubiqlang is legible to domain experts and robots
- names found from the domain resist drift — no synonym sprawl, no overload
- objects/operations discovered early compose later (the garden)
- a term you did not discover is a term you invent badly under deadline

## .the two things you discover
| kind | what | shaped as |
|------|------|-----------|
| domain-objects (dobjs) | nouns the domain holds — Surfer, SurfLesson, WaveReport | [...noun][state]? |
| domain-operations (dops) | verbs the domain performs — genSurfLesson, setSurferSkillLevel | [verb][...noun] |

## .how — the moves
loop expand→collect until converge (exhaust). moves:
1. listen to how folks talk — capture exact words from BOTH the expert (precise canonical term = your dobj/dop) and the layfolk (intuitive common word; reveals where jargon obscures). agree=strong candidate; diverge=a synonym/overload to settle. do not translate either — adopt
2. name from the motive — name from why it exists, not its mechanism
3. ask the five whys — ask "why?" ~5x; each why strips a layer of mechanism; the answer that no longer shifts is the buried motive. "reservation row"→why→"hold a slot"→why→"surfer keeps their spot in a lesson" = dobj SurfLesson, dop holdSurferSlot, buried 2 whys beneath a storage detail
4. decompose dimensionally — walk the product of orthogonal axes (howto.dimensional-decomposition); axes=attributes, cells=objects, forbidden=invariants
5. demonstrate the experience as a narrative, then distill to a bdd timeline — tell one concrete end-to-end story (raw narrative surfaces the domain in motion: nouns=dobjs, events=dops, state changes=attributes); then distill to given/when/then (given=precondition state, when=dop, then=the state after). narrative discovers; bdd refines
6. probe the lifecycle — states + the event that drives each move
7. hunt the relationships — refs, back-refs, natural key
8. vet the term — no synonym, no ambiguous overload; one word per concept

## .premier tactics
reach for these two first:
- dimensional decomposition — walk the product to surface objects, attributes, forbidden invariants
- narrative, then bdd timeline — demonstrate a concrete experience as a plain story, then distill to given/when/then; surfaces the domain in motion, catches dops a static object-list misses; bdd refines the dops + state transitions

## .the test — discovered, not invented
- domain expert recognizes it with no gloss
- names what IS or why, never how
- exactly one sense in the domain
- composes: object nests, operation chains

## .the caveat
discover what the domain holds today; do not invent speculative objects (rule.prefer.wet-over-dry)
a discovered gap is a note on record, not a mandate to build

## .see also
